From 9890b4afcc6a254de1d786f3669230400842525c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:21:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: smb1360: no thermal zone for the battery supply

The power supply core registers a thermal zone for every supply that
reports a temperature, so the battery appeared as thermal zone "battery"
next to Android's own battery temperature, and hardware-info apps
(AIDA64) listed it twice. Nothing reads the zone: Android's battery
service and thermal-engine (its battery charging action) use the power
supply itself. Set no_thermal for the battery supply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016iwHzV2tPonTxdceSkWZtS
---
 drivers/power/smb1360-charger-fg.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/smb1360-charger-fg.c b/drivers/power/smb1360-charger-fg.c
index 9c6b3c6c..6a4a0e06 100644
--- a/drivers/power/smb1360-charger-fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/smb1360-charger-fg.c
@@ -5640,6 +5640,12 @@ static int smb1360_probe(struct i2c_client *client,
 	chip->batt_psy.num_properties  = ARRAY_SIZE(smb1360_battery_properties);
 	chip->batt_psy.external_power_changed = smb1360_external_power_changed;
 	chip->batt_psy.property_is_writeable = smb1360_battery_is_writeable;
+	/*
+	 * No "battery" thermal zone: nothing reads it (Android's battery service and
+	 * thermal-engine use the power supply), and hardware-info apps listed the
+	 * battery temperature twice, once from the zone and once from Android.
+	 */
+	chip->batt_psy.no_thermal = true;
 
 	rc = power_supply_register(chip->dev, &chip->batt_psy);
 	if (rc < 0) {
